{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Encoding UTF8 'docs/workflow-format.md' | Select-Object -Skip 496 -First 40; Get-Content -Encoding UTF8 'out/final-20261011-173711/sources/11-sources-emails-2026-09-24-kickoff-questions-txt.md' | Select-Object -Skip 100 -First 40\"","aggregated_output":"| `is_tool_call` | Offer the global node to the dialogue model as a tool, not as a per-turn check |\r\n\r\n`__previous__` as a `target_node` or as `passthrough_default_transition` returns to the node that was interrupted.\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"global_nodes\": {\r\n    \"off_topic\": {\r\n      \"name\": \"off_topic\",\r\n      \"description\": \"Brings the caller back to the subject\",\r\n      \"condition\": { \"operator\": \"matches_intent\", \"description\": \"The user talks about something unrelated to their order\" },\r\n      \"task_message\": \"Redirect the caller to the subject.\",\r\n      \"on_enter\": { \"type\": \"tts\", \"text\": \"I can only help with your order. Let us continue.\" },\r\n      \"passthrough\": true,\r\n      \"passthrough_default_transition\": \"__previous__\",\r\n      \"excluded_nodes\": [\"goodbye\"],\r\n      \"transitions\": [\r\n        { \"target_node\": \"__previous__\", \"description\": \"always\", \"condition\": { \"operator\": \"always\" } }\r\n      ]\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nRules:\r\n\r\n- List terminal nodes in `excluded_nodes`, or the global node can loop.\r\n- Exclude nodes where an interrupt would do harm, for example an identity check.\r\n- For a plain redirect use a passthrough node with a fixed line. It is faster and more predictable than a model reply.\r\n- Use global nodes for interrupts that can happen anywhere. Do not copy the same transition into every node.\r\n\r\n## Extraction schema\r\n\r\n`extraction_schema` is an array on a node. After each user message the extraction model fills the listed variables from the conversation.\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"extraction_schema\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"order_number\",\r\n6. Silence. The analysis says three silences and then main menu. Is that the IVR rule or something you want specifically for the assistant?\r\n>> Burcu\r\n\r\n7. Service timeouts. If the debt service is slow, how long should we wait before we give up? And what does the caller hear while waiting?\r\n>> Honestly not defined yet. Mert owns the service side, I've asked him, he is on leave until the 5th. While waiting I think \"Bilgilerinizi kontrol ediyorum.\" is fine but let's confirm the timing with him. If a service returns an error, it's an agent, not the main menu: \"Şu anda işleminizi gerçekleştiremiyorum, sizi müşteri temsilcimize aktarıyorum.\"\r\n\r\n8. Third party calls (someone asking about a spouse's card).\r\n>> Burcu\r\n\r\n9. Statement week change: the analysis has the step but not the limits. How often can a customer change it, and does the assistant need to say the limit?\r\n>> Kerem\r\n\r\n10. Callers who speak another language.\r\n>> Burcu\r\n\r\n11. Agent requests. If the caller asks for a person right at the start, do we try to help first?\r\n>> For now no: transfer on the first request, no persuading. \"Sizi müşteri temsilcimize aktarıyorum.\" We might revisit once we see the numbers after go-live.\r\n\r\n12. (small one) Card names: in the analysis table some rows say \"Yıldız Gold\" and some \"Yıldız Altın\". Which one comes back from the service?\r\n>> Use whatever the card list service returns, don't translate. I'll fix the table. Btw we've seen a few cards where the name comes back empty from the service, in that case just introduce it by the last four digits (\"Sonu 4253 ile biten kartınıza ait …\").\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nDeniz\r\n\r\n--\r\nDeniz Arı\r\nSolutions Engineer, Freya\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
